# Complete Workflow Options & Variables (`WorkflowDef v2`)

Every `WorkflowDef` YAML file uses strict `deny_unknown_fields` validation and is verified by `acdd validate` (failing closed with `ACDD_WORKFLOW_SCHEMA_INVALID` on unknown or legacy keys).

- **Default workspace file**: `.acdd/workflows/default.yaml` (falls back to embedded `code` when absent).
- **Custom workflows folder**: `.acdd/workflows/<name>.yaml` (configured via `workflows_dirs:` in `acdd.yaml`).
- **Embedded workflows vs. reference templates**: 3 core workflows (`base`, `code`, `documentation`) are embedded in the binary; `audit`, `spec_planning`, and `hotfix` live in `skills/acdd/references/acdd-workflow-examples/`.

---

## 1. Top-level keys & inheritance

| Key | Type | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `version` | `2` (integer) | Required schema version (must be `2`). |
| `inherit` | string | Built-in workflow (`base`, `code`, `documentation`), `"none"`, or relative file path with optional SHA-256 pin. |
| `git` | object | Git isolation and worktree cleanup policy (`isolation`, `worktrees`). |
| `save` | string | Default save action on terminal root gates (`"none"` or `"commit"`). |
| `tags` | list or `null` | Allowed task tags (`"default"` always allowed; `code` adds `"docs"`). |
| `protected_paths` | list | Workspace-relative globs blocked from normal task writes. |
| `default_tools` | list | Default MCP tool allowlist for gates that omit `tools:`. |
| `modules` | object | Subsystem toggles and `DomainProvider` overrides (`domains.<id>`). |
| `limits` | object | Eight numeric resource and context ceilings (Section 2). |
| `roles` | map | Role execution modes, model hints, guidance, and `runner:` CLIs (Section 3). |
| `commands` | map | Named shell command templates in 4 YAML shapes (Section 4). |
| `scope_args_by_pattern` | map | Maps task scope globs to `{scope_target}` command arguments. |
| `proofs` | map | Reusable JSON Schema catalog referenced via `proof: <id>`. |
| `guidance` | map | Reusable instruction blocks (`string` or `{ description, criteria }`). |
| `contours` | map | Named audit dimensions (`{ description, criteria }`) for `review` gates. |
| `gate_templates` | map | Reusable gate macro blocks expanded via `use: <tpl_id>`. |
| `gates` | list | Replaces the inherited gate DAG completely (mutually exclusive with `gates_patch`). |
| `gates_patch` | list | Patches, inserts, or deletes inherited gates (forbidden with `inherit: none`). |

### `inherit:` & `git:` details

- **`inherit` values**: `"base"`, `"code"`, `"documentation"`, `"default"` (workspace `.acdd/workflows/default.yaml`), `"none"`, or `"<relpath>[:<sha256_prefix>]"`.
- **Content pin**: appending `:<7..64 hex chars>` fails closed if the parent file changes unexpectedly.
- **`git.isolation`**: `"worktree"` (isolated branch under `.worktrees/<run>`) or `"in_place"` (`--in-place` overrides this and neutralizes `save.post: commit` to `none`).
- **`git.worktrees`**: `"manual"` (user/agent manages worktrees) or `"managed"` (engine creates and cleans worktrees automatically).

---

## 2. `limits:` (all 8 resource ceilings)

| Field | Default (`base`) | Bounds |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `max_guidance_bytes` | `32768` (32 KiB) | Ceiling for Tier 1 `contract` + `guidance` via `tier1_cap = limits.max_guidance_bytes.min(response_hard_cap)` (`GUIDANCE_BUDGET_EXCEEDED`). |
| `max_log_bytes` | `1048576` (1 MiB) | Maximum persisted trace log file size per `acdd verify` run. |
| `max_capture_bytes` | `262144` (256 KiB) | Maximum stdout/stderr bytes captured in memory during command execution. |
| `max_line_bytes` | `65536` (64 KiB) | Single-line byte cap for streamed runner or command output. |
| `diagnostic_inline_bytes` | `4096` (4 KiB) | Tail length of `failed_trace_log_tail` inlined into `ClaimResp` Tier 2 on rework. |
| `max_metadata_bytes` | `2048` (2 KiB) | Metadata payload ceiling for gate and task records. |
| `max_trace_summary_bytes` | `2048` (2 KiB) | Stored summary size cap per verification trace. |
| `max_command_timeout_seconds` | `1800` (30 min) | Maximum allowed `timeout_seconds` for any gate or `verify` command. |

---

## 3. `roles.<id>` & headless runner variables

| Field | Type | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `mode` | string | `"subagent"` (default delegation) or `"inline"` (runs in coordinator session). |
| `reuse_on_reject` | bool | Hints `acdd run` to resume the same worker session when routing back on `fail` (`false` default). |
| `models` | list | Advisory ordered preference list (`"model"`, `"model:reasoning"`, `{ model, reasoning? }`). |
| `guidance` | string \| `null` | Role-level coordinator instruction note (`null` clears inherited note). |
| `runner` | string \| `null` | Shell CLI invoked by `acdd run`; receives rendered `ClaimResp` Markdown on `stdin`. |
| `prompt_template` | string \| `null` | Custom template rendered before writing to `runner`'s `stdin`. |

### Environment variables passed to `runner`

| Variable | Value |
| --- | --- |
| `ACDD_RUN_ID` | Active run UUID / ID |
| `ACDD_NODE_CURSOR` | Claimed gate cursor (`T1.build`, `blueprint_synthesis.synthesize`, ...) |
| `ACDD_CLAIM_REVISION` | Monotonic optimistic claim revision integer |
| `ACDD_WORKER_ID` | Assigned worker identity |
| `ACDD_AGENT_SESSION_ID` | Session ID for `reuse_on_reject` continuity |
| `ACDD_WORKTREE` | Absolute path to assigned worktree directory |
| `ACDD_STATE_DB` | Absolute path to `.acdd/state.sqlite` |
| `ACDD_CODE_DB` | Absolute path to `.acdd/code-map.sqlite` |
| `TRACEPARENT` | W3C Trace Context header for distributed telemetry |

---

## 4. `commands.<id>` forms & template variables

Each key under `commands:` accepts one of four forms (or `null` to clear an inherited slot):

1. **Abstract slot**: `{ abstract: true, description? }` (or `unbound: true`) — must be overridden by a child workflow before starting a run.
2. **Simple string**: `"cargo test --workspace"`
3. **Detailed object**:
   ```yaml
   commands:
     build_check:
       command: "cargo clippy {scope_target} --all-features -- -D warnings && cargo test {scope_target} {test_filter}"
       description: "Strict lint and scoped task tests"
       test_filter: "{test}"            # true | false | "-- {test}" | "{test}"
       timeout_seconds: 900
       scope_args_by_pattern:
         "src/**/*.rs": "--lib"
   ```
4. **Pattern-dispatched (`by_pattern`)**:
   ```yaml
   commands:
     build_check:
       by_pattern:
         "crates/**": "cargo test -p {scope_target} {test_filter}"
         "frontend/**": "npm test -- {test_filter}"
       description: "Dispatch verification by task scope"
   ```
   *(Also accepts a YAML list of `{ pattern, command, ... }` entries.)*

### Command & report placeholders

| Variable | Expanded in | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `{scope_target}` | `commands.<id>.command` | Matched value from `scope_args_by_pattern` for the task's `admitted_scope`. |
| `{file_stem}` | `scope_args_by_pattern` | File stem of matched path (`"tests/core.rs": "--test {file_stem}"` → `--test core`). |
| `{test_filter}` | `commands.<id>.command` | Expands `test_filter` template when `--test <filter>` is passed to `verify` (else empty). |
| `{test}` | `commands.<id>.test_filter` | Value of `--test <filter>` (`test_filter: "-- {test}"` → `-- my_test`). |
| `{run_id}` | `save.report` | Active run ID. |
| `{run_name}` | `save.report` | Human-readable run slug/name. |
| `{gate_id}` | `save.report` | Current gate ID. |
| `{spec_id}` | `save.report` | Spec document ID (when started from a spec). |

---

## 5. Gate & `- tasks:` fields

### 5.1 Structure & routing

| Field | Applies to | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | Gate | Unique gate ID inside its parent scope (omitted on anonymous `- tasks:` blocks). |
| `gates` | Container | Nested child gates inside this container. |
| `tasks` | Track | `{ when?, gates: [...] }` — instantiates child gates per non-cancelled task. |
| `when` | Task gate / track | Boolean tag filter: `tag`, `!tag`, `&`/`+` (AND), `\|` (OR), `( ... )` (forbidden on root gates). |
| `use` | Gate | Expands a named template from `gate_templates`. |
| `pass` | Gate | Next sibling gate ID on pass (defaults to next sibling in YAML order). |
| `fail` | Review / command | Target sibling gate ID on `defect` rejection or command failure. |
| `fail_drift` | Review gate | Target sibling gate ID (e.g. `rearchitect`) on `architectural_drift` (`context_reset_required: true`). |

### 5.2 Execution, checks & context

| Field | Applies to | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `role` | Role gate | Worker role ID from `roles:` (`architect`, `builder`, `independent_reviewer`, `auditor`). |
| `command` | Command gate | Key from `commands:` executed during `acdd verify` / `acdd run`. |
| `call` / `with` | Action gate | Runs `<domain>.<action>` on a `DomainProvider` with JSON `with: { ... }` payload. |
| `checks` | Any verified gate | List of `"<domain>.<check>"` or `{ check, with }` (`code.seam`, `code.lint`, `docs.links`, `docs.specs`). |
| `context` | Role gate | Ordered list of `DomainProvider` lenses injected into `ClaimResp` Tier 6. |
| `tools` | Role gate | Replaces `default_tools` for this gate (also supports `tools_add` / `tools_remove`). |
| `guidance` | Any gate | Keys from `guidance:` or `{ inline: "..." }` blocks injected into `ClaimResp.guidance`. |
| `contours` | Review gate | List of `contours:` keys audited by `independent_reviewer`. |
| `scope` | Explicit gate | List of workspace-relative globs (e.g. `polish` admitting `docs/**`, `README.md`). |

- **Available `context:` lenses**: `paths.instructions`, `paths.adrs`, `paths.<name>`, `specs.<collection>`, `docs.invariants`, `docs.workspace_config`, `code.symbols`, `code.tests`, `code.external_callers`.

### 5.3 Proofs, dependencies & persistence

| Field | Applies to | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `proof` | Any gate | Validation mode: `"none"`, `"command"`, `"call"`, `"review"`, `"<catalog_id>"`, or `{ scheme }`. |
| `need` | Any gate | Sibling/predecessor cursors that must complete with matching `accepted_tree`. |
| `independent_from` | Review / deliver | Gate cursors (e.g. `[build]`, `[polish, "tasks.build"]`) whose `worker_id` cannot match this claimer. |
| `max_attempts` | Any gate | Retry ceiling before escalation (default `3`). |
| `receipt` | Terminal gate | `true` closes the task/run container and records `ArtifactKind::Proof`. |
| `save` | Any gate | Persistence policy (`"none"`, `"commit"`, `"snapshot"`, or object). |

- **`proof:` values**: `"review"` requires `role` and non-empty `contours`; `{ scheme: <JSON Schema> }` validates custom JSON proof payloads inline.
- **`save:` object keys**: `{ post?, immutable?, archive?, prune?, report? }`:
  - `post: "snapshot"` creates refs under `refs/acdd/snapshots/<run_id>/<task_ref>/r<rev>` without moving `HEAD` (leaf task gates only).
  - `report:` writes Markdown/JSON templates strictly under `.acdd/reports/`.
